>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Schulze</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Borsdorf</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ng</surname><given-names>SW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Solution <sup>13</sup>C and <sup>119</sup>Sn NMR spectroscopic Investigations on triorganotin derivatives of isothiazol-3(2H)-one 1,1-dioxides and their adducts with O-donor ligands</article-title><source><italic>Journal f&#x000fc;r Praktische Chemie</italic></source><year>1995</year><volume>337</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>242</fpage><lpage>244</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B6c"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>N&#x000e1;dvornik</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hol&#x0010d;ek</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Hand&#x000ed;&#x00159;</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Ly&#x0010d;ka</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The<sup>13</sup>C and <sup>119</sup>Sn NMR spectra of some four- and five-coordinate tri-n-butyltin(IV) compounds</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Organometallic Chemistry</italic></source><year>1984</year><volume>275</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>43</fpage><lpage>51</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Addison</surname><given-names>AW</given-names></name><name><surname>Rao</surname><given-names>TN</given-names></name><name><surname>Reedijk</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Van Rijn</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Verschoor</surname><given-names>GC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Synthesis, structure, and spectroscopic properties of copper(II) compounds containing nitrogen-sulphur donor ligands; the crystal and molecular structure of aq